# ── AutoMax: tokens and keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here is mandatory for the platform itself. AutoMax API tokens are
# self-issued and free (`automax tokens create`). Check status: `automax doctor`.
#
#   mandatory  only when the feature next to it is used
#   one-of     agents need ANY ONE of the four options in the Agents block
#   optional   turns on an integration
#   ci-only    GitHub Actions secrets, never needed locally

# ── Database (mandatory: none; DATABASE_URL only when DB_DRIVER=postgres) ─────
DB_DRIVER=sqlite
SQLITE_PATH=.automax/automax.db
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://automax:automax@localhost:5432/automax

# ── Web server (`automax serve`) — SESSION_SECRET mandatory for serve only ────
PORT=4444
HOST=127.0.0.1
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-32-chars-minimum-please   # openssl rand -hex 32
# AUTOMAX_PUBLIC_URL=https://automax.example.com
# AUTH_DISABLED=1   # local dev only

# Where projects and run artifacts live (defaults shown)
# AUTOMAX_PROJECTS_DIR=projects
# AUTOMAX_ARTIFACTS_DIR=.automax/runs

# ── Agents (one-of; every agent command also has --dry-run and --adapter fake) ─
# Pick ONE way for agents to reach a model. Auto-detection order when unset:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY → `claude` CLI on PATH → `codex` CLI on PATH → OPENAI_API_KEY → fake
# AUTOMAX_LLM_PROVIDER=claude-code      # claude | claude-code | codex | openai-compatible | fake
#
# 1) Claude via API key (billed by Anthropic)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# 2) Claude Code CLI login — no key needed: `npm i -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code && claude login`
#    (adapter claude-code; optional AUTOMAX_CLAUDE_CODE_MODEL=... to pin a model)
#
# 3) Codex CLI login — no key needed: `npm i -g @openai/codex && codex login`
#    (adapter codex; optional AUTOMAX_CODEX_MODEL=... to pin a model)
#
# 4) Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (billed by the provider)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=                      # optional: Azure, Ollama, vLLM, ...

# ── Integrations (optional; project yaml stores only the variable NAMES) ──────
# GITHUB_TOKEN=            # check runs, PR comments, issues
# JIRA_EMAIL=              # Jira Cloud basic auth
# JIRA_API_TOKEN=

# ── AutoMax's own token (optional, free): MCP over HTTP and CI ingest ─────────
# AUTOMAX_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4444
# AUTOMAX_TOKEN=amx_...    # automax tokens create --user <name> --scopes runs:ingest,runs:read

# ── CI-only GitHub secrets (never needed locally) ────────────────────────────
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_AUTOMAX_DOCS   docs deploy (Firebase Hosting)
# NPM_TOKEN                               publishing @automax/* packages
